  "configuration_id": "config_021",
  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the dominant uncertainty is whether a basic multimodal (RNA + image) pipeline is viable and what level of performance to expect. Config_021 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, aggregation=None, fusion=concat) is the simplest well-motivated multimodal baseline: it uses the most standard and interpretable components on each axis (PCA for RNA, ResNet50 for image, no aggregation needed for a single profile, and plain concatenation for fusion). This establishes a clear reference point with minimal confounding complexity. If it performs well, it confirms multimodality is promising and subsequent experiments can isolate which added complexity (multiprofile, learned encoders, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion) actually helps. If it underperforms, we learn early that the basic multimodal signal is weak and should pivot toward unimodal baselines or stronger encoders. Choosing this over a more complex config avoids attributing any (lack of) performance to multiple simultaneous design choices, and choosing it over a unimodal config directly tests the core hypothesis of this multimodal study while still serving as a ceiling for what a unimodal model could achieve with the same image encoder."
}

